BSP-Yocto-NXP-i.MX95-ALPHA1                                           2025-05-28
================================================================================
- Linux kernel v6.6.52-2.2.0-phy13 (LTS kernel)
- U-Boot v2024.04-2.2.0-phy6
- System Manager 6.6.52-2.2.0-phy1
- Optional Executable Image 6.6.52-2.2.0-phy1
- Yocto 5.0.9 (scarthgap)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working correctly.

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-headless-image
- phytec-qt6demo-image
- phytec-vision-image

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04 64-bit

Supported Machines:
-------------------
imx95-libra-fpsc-1

Features:
---------
- Boot from e.MMC
- Boot from SD card
- Boot via USB serial download (uuu)
- LVDS display support
- GPU support
- RTC support
- Debug UART support
- GBit Ethernet support (SoM + Carrier board)
- Power Management support (suspend + frequency scaling)
- U-Boot standard boot (https://docs.u-boot.org/en/v2024.04/develop/bootstd.html#u-boot-standard-boot)
- NPU support
- Camera support
    * VM-016 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-017 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-020 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
- ISP support (Debayer, AEC, AWB)

Known Issues and Limitations:
-----------------------------
- GPU performance may be very low; As of release date, NXP is investigating
  this issue as it is present on their EVK as well.
- U-Boot does not support USB host
- Sporadic artifacts when capturing camera images with yavta

